=You are reading the objections buyers left under competitor review videos. Everything below has already been counted - do not restate the numbers, do not recount them, and do not add any figure that is not here.

Our product: {{ $('Settings').first().json.your_brand }}

The themes, largest first:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.themes, null, 1) }}

Products people named when they said they left:
{{ JSON.stringify($json.alternatives, null, 1) }}

Answer in exactly this shape, one line per theme, using the theme keys given above and nothing else:
SUMMARY: two sentences on what the comment sections say buyers actually care about, and which theme is worth acting on first.
THEME <key>: one sentence on what this group of comments is really objecting to, in the buyer's own terms.

Write about what people said, not about the video or the channel. If a theme is small enough that it could be three loud people, say so rather than presenting it as a trend. No preamble, no bullet points, no sign-off.

